  "about": "The stock PRO-800's CC numbers (Behringer's chart: a parameter on CC 8 + i with its fine part on 80 + i, the buttons from 48), for a controller template made for the stock synth. What stock has and this firmware hasn't (velocity amounts, envelope shapes, the LFO's shape and speed range, the bender and mod wheel targets) is left out, and so is the filter's keyboard tracking (CC 60: how stock spreads its three values isn't known), and so are the fine parts on 100 and 101, which are RPN numbers here. CC A (11 by default) takes CC 11 before the map: set CC A to another number to have stock's Freq B there. CC 74 is LFO 1 to pitch here, as on stock (in the 8CH and MPE modes it stays each voice's Timbre).",
